"The Rain Gauge"
Lakshmi lived in a small village where most people were farmers. Every year the farmers argued about how much rain had fallen. One day Lakshmi's science teacher showed the class how to make a rain gauge from a plastic bottle and a ruler. Lakshmi made one and placed it in an open space behind her house, away from trees. Each morning she measured the water, wrote the number in a notebook and emptied the bottle. At the end of the monsoon, she showed her notebook at the village meeting. The farmers were surprised to see that July had received twice as much rain as June. From then on, they asked Lakshmi before deciding when to sow their seeds.

