"Honeybees"
Honeybees live together in large groups called colonies. A colony has one queen, a few hundred drones and thousands of worker bees. The queen lays all the eggs. The worker bees, which are all female, do almost every other job. They clean the hive, feed the young bees, guard the entrance and collect nectar and pollen from flowers. When a worker finds a good patch of flowers, she returns to the hive and performs a special 'waggle dance'. The direction and length of the dance tell the other bees where the flowers are. While collecting nectar, bees carry pollen from one flower to another. This helps plants produce fruits and seeds, so bees are very important for farmers.

