"The Boy from Rameswaram"
A. P. J. Abdul Kalam was born in 1931 in Rameswaram, a small town on an island in Tamil Nadu. His family was not rich, so as a young boy he helped by distributing newspapers early in the morning before school. He loved watching birds fly and wondered how they could rise so easily into the sky. His teachers noticed his curiosity and encouraged him to study hard. Kalam later became a scientist and worked on India's space and missile programmes. In 2002 he became the President of India. Even then, he loved meeting students and often told them to dream big and work hard to make their dreams come true.

