"The Mangrove Forest"
The Sundarbans is a huge mangrove forest where the rivers Ganga and Brahmaputra meet the Bay of Bengal. Mangroves are trees that can grow in salty water. Their roots grow above the mud like thin fingers so that they can breathe when the tide is high. The forest protects villages along the coast because the thick trees slow down strong winds and waves during storms. The Sundarbans is famous as the home of the Royal Bengal tiger, which is a good swimmer. Crocodiles, deer, monkeys and many kinds of birds also live there. Today people are working to protect the forest, because without it both the animals and the villagers would be in danger.

