"Kites over Ahmedabad"
In January, on the festival of Makar Sankranti, the sky over Ahmedabad fills with thousands of colourful kites. Weeks before the festival, families buy paper kites and spools of strong string called 'manja'. On the festival day, people climb onto their rooftops early in the morning. Neighbours shout 'Kai po che!' whenever they cut someone else's kite. Children run through the lanes to catch the kites that float down. In the evening, some people fly paper lanterns that glow in the dark sky. Doctors and animal lovers also remind everyone to be careful, because sharp kite strings can hurt birds. Many volunteers set up camps to treat injured birds during the festival.

