"The Village Library"
There was no library in Sonpur, so the children had very few books to read. Ramesh, a retired teacher, decided to do something about it. He cleaned an empty room in the panchayat building and put up a sign that said 'Library – Open to All'. At first he had only his own fifty books. Then he wrote letters to his old students, who were now living in different cities. Parcels of books began to arrive every week. Soon the room had more than a thousand books. Children came every evening after school, and even some grandparents learned to read there. Ramesh smiled and said, 'A book is a friend that never leaves you.'

