"The Clever Shepherd"
A shepherd boy named Bhola took his goats to graze near a forest every day. One afternoon he saw dark clouds and heard the river roaring louder than usual. Bhola noticed that the water was rising quickly and that the small bridge to the village was in danger. Instead of running home alone, he gathered his goats and led them to a hill. Then he climbed a tall tree and waved his red cloth to warn the people working in the fields. The farmers saw the signal and moved to higher ground just before the river flooded the fields. That evening the whole village thanked Bhola for his presence of mind.

