"Grandmother's Garden"
Every summer holiday, Neha visited her grandmother in Nashik. Behind the house was a small garden full of tomatoes, chillies, brinjals and a big guava tree. Grandmother woke up at sunrise to water the plants, and Neha soon began to help her. She learned that dried leaves and vegetable peels could be put in a pit to make compost, a natural manure for the soil. Grandmother never used chemical sprays. Instead, she planted marigold flowers between the vegetables to keep some insects away. By the end of the holiday, Neha had planted her own row of spinach. When she went home, she started a small kitchen garden on her balcony.

